WEBVTT

00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:14,400
It's tumeric essential oil with the MSO rubbed right on my

00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:19,400
papyrus area, okay, to do three times a day.

00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:30,660
So, tumeric essential oil, so I don't think so.

00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:34,260
So as I think about it, okay, so what are the benefits of tumeric?

00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:40,860
tumeric is a flavonoid, and the benefit is that it has cancer-killing

00:00:40,860 --> 00:00:45,260
properties, so tumeric is curcumin, remember, has cancer-killing

00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:46,780
properties in itself.

00:00:46,780 --> 00:00:52,460
It's anti-inflammatory has all these benefits, but the essential oil

00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:58,940
of curcumin, tumeric, I don't know, that's going to be more of an

00:00:58,940 --> 00:01:00,220
alkaloid.

00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:05,180
I don't know if that has the same properties of the whole plant

00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:14,060
flavonoid, so I don't know that that is, it probably wouldn't hurt

00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:18,700
anything if you did it three times a day, and the DMSO itself

00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:23,820
can be anti-inflammatory, so I don't think that's a wrong

00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:29,260
approach, but I don't think you can count that as the benefits of

00:01:29,260 --> 00:01:33,900
curcumin, because I don't know much curcumin is actually

00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:38,300
in the tumeric essential oil. Most essential oils are

00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:44,700
alkaloids, and they have benefits, but I don't think the exact same benefit

00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:49,420
of the whole plant, so I don't think there's anything wrong with that,

00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:53,900
to answer your question, but I don't know that you're getting the same

00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:57,900
benefit of taking tumeric.

